  "id": "deterrence",
  "term": "deterrence",
  "definition": "Deterrence is the idea that people are more likely to follow rules when they believe violations will bring penalties. In this source, it is reflected in how awareness of the law shapes behavior through perceived certainty and perceived severity of sanctions, with certainty having the stronger influence.",
